Memelang
Memelang is a terse query language that substantially reduces compute costs for LLMs emitting billions of SQL queries daily. Low-token Memelang is emitted as an intermediate representation which is then programatically translated into higher-token SQL for the database. Example:
Memelang (20 tokens)
roles actor :$a="Mark Hamill";movie _;@ @ @;actor !$a
SQL (36 tokens)
SELECT x.actor,x.movie,y.movie,y.actor FROM roles AS x,roles AS y WHERE x.actor='Mark Hamill' AND y.id!=x.id AND y.movie=x.movie
